      "value": "@{5a7ac88bf5a5c52c08064fb9|full_name}: The two things that you've described are clear to me, but I do appreciate your help and maybe it is useful to others. To clarify my points, here is a more detailed description:\n\nI provided two examples that have the wrong marking. The second one is a good example because it was already solved in sdk 3.2.0 or earlier. The first one is also relevant, because I saw Tupper going through Cannys when the beta went live, but mine slipped through. Right now it isn't even tracked so that is definitely wrong. \n\nI tagged Tupper in the comments to mention that, but to no success. So this isn't ideal, I could probably keep tagging different people in the comments but since they'd always be individuals, they might not see it or are the wrong people to reach out to, so I'd essentially just spam others. \n\nThere are probably better solutions than what we have right now to keep Canny a bit more clean. Some that are harder to implement (allow me to mark my own Cannys, maybe with Staff reviewing that marking then), and some that are easier to implement like a Discord channel where things like that can be requested and someone will do it for me.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
