  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-07-01T08:26:58.318Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I often find a Canny which is already implemented/solved (but not marked as such). Or my Canny was implemented 1:1 but did not receive any flag. A great example for this is https://feedback.vrchat.com/vrchat-udon-closed-alpha-feedback/p/add-onavatarchanged-event which was silently added to the new SDK, even with the exact name, but isn't even marked as \"Tracked\" yet. It wasn't mentioned in the release notes either, so I only found it by accident.\n\nThis is especially confusing when the Canny describes a bug that appears to be unsolved, but was solved in a newer version already, so we just need to update our SDK. Example: https://feedback.vrchat.com/sdk-bug-reports/p/sdk-login-panel-crashes-if-you-submit-a-blank-userpassword\n\nWe cannot mark our own Cannys as solved, so there should be a way how we can submit a Canny to someone from VRChat to get it marked as such. Maybe a channel on the VRChat discord where we can drop Canny links to request a status update?",
